<BaseLayout
  title="How HVAC Boot Camp Works | Current Course and Unit 1 Preview"
  description="See exactly how the existing HVAC Boot Camp is delivered in Moodle, what the textbook and quizzes involve, and how the new Unit 1 preview differs."
>
  <div class="standard-page refreshed-how">
    <section class="page-hero"><div class="page-hero-inner narrow-hero"><p class="eyebrow">How Boot Camp works</p><h1>Study online. <span>Build understanding step by step.</span></h1><p>Know the format before you enroll: the paid Boot Camp is a 27-module Moodle course with textbook reading, Ron's teaching videos, and quizzes.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/hvac-boot-camp/">Explore the course</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/unit-1-prototype/">See the redesign preview</a></div></div></section>

    <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="today-title"><div class="page-shell">
      <div class="section-heading center"><p class="eyebrow">The paid course today</p><h2 id="today-title">A clear sequence of topics, with work to do in each module.</h2><p>Boot Camp starts at the fundamentals and moves through refrigeration, systems, electricity, heating, and heat pumps. You can study online around your schedule.</p></div>
      <div class="how-steps">
        <article><span>01</span><div><p class="step-label">Enroll</p><h3>Access the course in Moodle</h3><p>The current course and student login live at hvactraining.academy. Enrollment is handled through the existing website.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>02</span><div><p class="step-label">Read and watch</p><h3>Work with the textbook and Ron's videos</h3><p>The course uses <em>Residential Construction Academy HVAC, 2nd Edition</em> by Eugene Silberstein, purchased separately, alongside online video instruction.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>03</span><div><p class="step-label">Check your learning</p><h3>Take quizzes as you progress</h3><p>Use the questions to find the topics you need to revisit. Some modules include formulas and conversions that take practice.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>04</span><div><p class="step-label">Apply the foundation</p><h3>Keep learning with supervision</h3><p>Bring your questions and technical vocabulary into conversations with employers and experienced technicians. Practical competence grows in the field.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="page-section soft-section" aria-labelledby="next-title"><div class="page-shell preview-split">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The course experience in development</p><h2 id="next-title">Try the new Unit 1 as a free preview.</h2><p>The recovered five-part demo explores cooling, heat, state changes, sensible and latent heat, and pressure. It has videos, a visual exercise, and immediate knowledge checks.</p><p class="preview-boundary"><strong>What you are previewing:</strong> a proposed lesson format. It does not save student progress or represent the full paid Boot Camp. The redesign is still being built.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/unit-1-prototype/">Open Unit 1</a></div>
      <div class="comparison-card"><p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p><div><strong>Boot Camp today</strong><span>27 modules · Moodle · textbook reading · videos · quizzes</span></div><div><strong>Unit 1 preview</strong><span>Five sections · short videos · visual interaction · knowledge checks · no account</span></div><p>Try the preview to help shape what comes next; use the current course description to make an enrollment decision today.</p></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="fit-title"><div class="page-shell">
      <div class="section-heading center"><p class="eyebrow">Set the right expectation</p><h2 id="fit-title">Online training is one part of becoming a technician.</h2><p>Boot Camp can build an understanding of the systems and language. Employers determine hiring, and safe hands-on work requires training and supervision on real equipment.</p></div>
      <div class="outcome-grid"><article><span>Technical</span><h3>Start with principles</h3><p>Understand heat, refrigerant, airflow, electrical controls, tools, and equipment.</p></article><article><span>Instructor</span><h3>Hear from Ron</h3><p>His video lessons explain the concepts; <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> with a course question.</p></article><article><span>Field</span><h3>Practice with supervision</h3><p>Use what you learned to ask better questions and build real skill alongside experienced people.</p></article></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="page-section final-cta"><div class="page-shell"><p class="eyebrow">Explore before deciding</p><h2>See the topics and the price.</h2><p>Review the 27-module curriculum, the full cost, and the new Unit 1 preview at your own pace.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/hvac-boot-camp/">Course details</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/pricing/">Pricing</a></div></div></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
